924	 * wiki's `dedicated.yaml` reference has exactly one relevant key,
925	 * `CustomScenario`, and it takes a SINGLE local folder name, not a Workshop
926	 * id or a list. So unlike every other family here, Empyrion can only have
927	 * ONE active Workshop scenario at a time — attempting a second install while
928	 * one is already active is refused rather than silently replacing it.
929	 *
930	 * Mechanism: `steamcmd workshop_download_item` (Valve's own tool, run inside
931	 * the customer's own container — bitr/empyrion-server documents a generic
932	 * `STEAMCMD=` passthrough env var for exactly this kind of one-off command)
933	 * fetches the scenario into the container's own workshop content cache; we
934	 * then copy it into `Content/Scenarios/` under a fixed name and point
935	 * `dedicated.yaml`'s `CustomScenario` at it.
936	 *
937	 * CONFIDENCE NOTE: the exact internal path layout under this image's mounted
938	 * volume (`/opt/empyrion` on the host, `/home/user/Steam` in the container)
939	 * is discovered at run time via `find` rather than hardcoded, because no
940	 * official source documents it precisely — if `dedicated.yaml` or
941	 * `Content/Scenarios` can't be located, this fails honestly instead of
942	 * guessing a path and silently writing nothing (or writing to the wrong
943	 * place).
944	 */
945	const EMPYRION_APPID = WORKSHOP_APPID.empyrion;
